WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:15.479
looked where Maggie was pointing.

2
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.520
A teenage boy had just walked up behind the lemonade stand.

3
00:00:20.481 --> 00:00:25.102
He was wearing jeans and a black T-shirt, and he had a tattoo of a snake on his

4
00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:28.643
arm. "It's okay, Maggie," Henry said quickly.

5
00:00:29.503 --> 00:00:32.744
The teenager looked pretty tough, and Henry didn't want to cause trouble.

6
00:00:33.636 --> 00:00:35.397
"I'm sure he wasn't spying on us."

7
00:00:36.457 --> 00:00:37.278
Maggie frowned.

8
00:00:37.298 --> 00:00:38.358
"How do you know?

9
00:00:39.258 --> 00:00:44.321
Maybe he's building a float for the parade, and he was eavesdropping so he can steal our ideas."

10
00:00:45.441 --> 00:00:46.562
The teenager laughed.

11
00:00:47.562 --> 00:00:51.604
"Actually, my rock band is entering a float.

12
00:00:52.564 --> 00:00:54.725
But we're not doing any silly lemon stuff.

13
00:00:55.725 --> 00:00:58.527
We're going to make our float look like a concert stage.

14
00:00:59.627 --> 00:01:01.748
Then we're going to play our music during the parade.

15
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:03.464
It will be awesome!"

16
00:01:03.485 --> 00:01:05.625
"Do you live in Belltown?"

17
00:01:05.785 --> 00:01:06.546
Henry asked.

18
00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:10.387
"I moved here at the beginning of the summer," the teenager said.

19
00:01:10.407 --> 00:01:14.449
"My name is Stan, but everyone calls me Snake."

20
00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.750
"Welcome to Belltown, Snake."

21
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.811
Cole poured a cup of lemonade.

22
00:01:18.831 --> 00:01:23.753
"Here's some lemonade—on the house."

23
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:27.395
"Thanks." Snake drank the lemonade.

24
00:01:27.415 --> 00:01:30.576
"Maybe my band will stop by later to buy more.

25
00:01:31.456 --> 00:01:33.697
We'll probably be thirsty after we practice.

26
00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:36.117
That reminds me—I have to go."

27
00:01:38.238 --> 00:01:40.118
Soon there were no customers in sight.

28
00:01:40.138 --> 00:01:44.780
"Hey, Nathan, can you watch the lemonade stand for a while?"

29
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:45.780
Henry asked.

30
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.161
"We should go work on our float.

31
00:01:48.721 --> 00:01:51.502
We only have two more days to finish it."

32
00:01:51.522 --> 00:01:53.662
"Yeah." Maggie picked up the laptop.

33
00:01:53.682 --> 00:01:56.643
"Plus, my mom doesn't know I have her computer."

34
00:01:56.663 --> 00:01:59.204
"Sure," Nathan said.

35
00:01:59.224 --> 00:02:00.264
"Have fun."

36
00:02:05.408 --> 00:02:07.590
The papier-mâché lemon was in Maggie's house.

37
00:02:08.991 --> 00:02:12.333
When it was finished, the kids were planning to attach it to a garden cart.

38
00:02:13.194 --> 00:02:15.956
Maggie's father would pull the cart behind his lawn tractor.

39
00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:18.718
"It looks awesome," Cole said.

40
00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.961
"But we still need to attach Sherlock Holmes' hat."

41
00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:25.003
Maggie dug into their craft supply box.

42
00:02:25.784 --> 00:02:26.984
"I think we're out of glue."

43
00:02:27.004 --> 00:02:29.626
"I'll go buy some," Henry offered.

44
00:02:29.646 --> 00:02:31.428
"You guys can keep working."

45
00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:35.853
Henry's house was right next door.

46
00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:39.273
He grabbed his bike and rode toward Main Street.

47
00:02:40.254 --> 00:02:42.294
On the way there, he heard loud rock music.

48
00:02:43.435 --> 00:02:45.435
It was coming from the garage of a nearby house.

49
00:02:46.496 --> 00:02:49.817
The garage door was open, so Henry stopped and looked in.

50
00:02:50.817 --> 00:02:53.057
Four teenagers were inside playing instruments.

51
00:02:54.138 --> 00:02:55.578
One of the musicians was Snake.

52
00:02:56.198 --> 00:02:57.979
There were two other boys and a girl.

53
00:03:00.039 --> 00:03:01.400
Snake saw Henry looking in.

54
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.961
He held up a hand, and the band stopped playing.

55
00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:08.423
The other three teens stared at Henry.

56
00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:12.444
Henry knew the drummer's name was Eddie and that this was his house.

57
00:03:13.405 --> 00:03:16.666
He also recognized the other two teens as students from the high school.

58
00:03:17.527 --> 00:03:18.927
But he didn't know any of them well.

59
00:03:18.947 --> 00:03:23.069
"Hey, it's the lemonade kid," Snake called with a smile.

60
00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:24.790
"Did you bring us a drink?"

61
00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.031
"No," Henry said.

62
00:03:27.051 --> 00:03:29.052
"I like your music, though."

63
00:03:30.048 --> 00:03:32.349
"Cool," one of the other boys said with a grin.

64
00:03:32.369 --> 00:03:34.089
"You have good taste."

65
00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:36.430
Henry glanced at the girl.

66
00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.590
He was pretty sure her name was Jade.

67
00:03:39.511 --> 00:03:41.891
She was ignoring everyone else as she tuned her guitar.

68
00:03:41.911 --> 00:03:44.652
"Are you here to spy on us, Lemonade Kid?"

69
00:03:45.632 --> 00:03:47.873
Snake laughed and glanced at the others with a grin.

70
00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.554
"He and his friends are making a float too."

71
00:03:50.574 --> 00:03:53.354
"Uh-oh," Eddie said.

72
00:03:53.374 --> 00:03:56.675
"So he's our competition for the prizes, huh?"

73
00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:59.476
"No way," the other boy said.

74
00:04:00.232 --> 00:04:01.693
"Our float is going to be awesome!

75
00:04:01.973 --> 00:04:02.894
We'll win for sure."

76
00:04:03.835 --> 00:04:05.756
Jade looked up from her guitar with a frown.

77
00:04:05.776 --> 00:04:08.318
"Can we get back to practicing?"

78
00:04:08.638 --> 00:04:09.118
she said.

79
00:04:09.138 --> 00:04:11.300
"I have to go to work soon."

80
00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.121
"Okay, okay."

81
00:04:13.481 --> 00:04:15.102
Snake strummed his bass guitar.

82
00:04:15.123 --> 00:04:17.864
"See you at the parade, Lemonade Kid."

83
00:04:17.884 --> 00:04:19.546
"See you."

84
00:04:20.306 --> 00:04:22.528
Henry hurried on as the music started again.

85
00:04:30.032 --> 00:04:31.793
"May I be excused, Mom?"

86
00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:32.813
Henry asked.

87
00:04:33.793 --> 00:04:36.274
It was the next day, and he'd just finished eating lunch.

88
00:04:36.294 --> 00:04:39.235
"Of course," his mother said.

89
00:04:39.255 --> 00:04:41.236
"Put your dishes in the sink.

90
00:04:42.256 --> 00:04:44.877
Are you going back to Maggie's house to work on your float?"

91
00:04:45.817 --> 00:04:48.038
Henry carried his plate and glass to the sink.

92
00:04:48.998 --> 00:04:50.919
"No, we worked on it all morning.

93
00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:55.220
I'm supposed to meet Maggie and Cole at the lemonade stand."

94
00:04:57.492 --> 00:05:00.635
When Henry reached the lemonade stand, his friends were already there.

95
00:05:01.295 --> 00:05:03.077
Maggie had her mother's laptop again.

96
00:05:03.097 --> 00:05:04.798
"What are you doing?"

97
00:05:04.998 --> 00:05:05.819
Henry asked her.

98
00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:10.703
"I want to leave a comment on the town website about our float," Maggie said.

99
00:05:10.723 --> 00:05:13.786
"Then people will look for us during the parade."

100
00:05:13.806 --> 00:05:16.348
"Are a lot of people leaving comments?"

101
00:05:16.688 --> 00:05:17.489
Cole asked.

102
00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.913
He and Henry watched as Maggie scrolled down to the comment section.

103
00:05:23.094 --> 00:05:25.616
Henry's eyes widened when he saw the latest comment.

104
00:05:26.364 --> 00:05:27.326
"Look at that!"

105
00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:28.348
he exclaimed.

106
00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.073
The comment was typed in capital letters.

107
00:05:32.075 --> 00:05:33.818
THE SUMMER PARADE IS FOR LOSERS.

108
00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.603
THE MAYOR SHOULD CANCEL IT—OR ELSE!
